IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-act`

-- Tests for the Act (ss 1 to 13).  Figures read off the text: two years (ss 8(1) and 8(3)),
-- the equivalent in Singapore dollars fixed by order (s 6(4)).

§ `Tests -- the Act`

§§ `2. Interpretation`

#ASSERT `the arbitrator is the court` (`Arbitration Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the arbitrator is the court` (`Arbitration Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the arbitrator is the court` (`Arbitration Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `3. Conventions to have force of law`

-- Force of Law Facts: the provisions relate to rights and liabilities of the persons named, the carriage is carriage by air
-- to which the Convention applies, the nationality of the aircraft.
#ASSERT `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore in relation to the carriage` (`Force of Law Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, "Singapore")
-- irrespective of the nationality of the aircraft
#ASSERT `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore in relation to the carriage` (`Force of Law Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, "France")
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore in relation to the carriage` (`Force of Law Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, "Singapore")
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore in relation to the carriage` (`Force of Law Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, "Singapore")
#ASSERT `the authentic French text prevails` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the authentic French text prevails` FALSE

§§ `4. High Contracting Parties`

-- State Facts: ratified or acceded, party in respect of the territory, availed itself of the Additional Protocol.
#ASSERT `the State is a High Contracting Party to the Convention` (`State Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the State is a High Contracting Party to the Convention` (`State Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the High Contracting Party in respect of the territory` (`State Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `this Act applies to the High Contracting Party in respect of the territory` (`State Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `this Act applies to the High Contracting Party in respect of the territory` (`State Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT `this Act applies to carriage performed directly by the High Contracting Party` (`State Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `this Act applies to carriage performed directly by the High Contracting Party` (`State Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this Act applies to carriage performed directly by the High Contracting Party` (`State Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT `Article 40A(2) extends the reference to include the territory` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 40A(2) extends the reference to include the territory` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 40A(2) extends the reference to include the territory` FALSE FALSE

§§ `5. Fatal accidents`

#ASSERT `the occurrence is a wrongful act, neglect or default for the purposes of section 20 of the Civil Law Act 1909` (`Passenger Accident Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the occurrence is a wrongful act, neglect or default for the purposes of section 20 of the Civil Law Act 1909` (`Passenger Accident Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `6. Limitations of liability`

#ASSERT `the limitations on liability in Article 22 apply whatever the nature of the proceedings by which liability may be enforced`

-- Limited Proceedings Facts: the proceedings enforce a liability limited by Article 22, the liability is or may be partly
-- enforceable elsewhere, the amounts awarded or recoverable in those other proceedings.
#ASSERT `the amount still recoverable within the limit for each passenger` 250_000 (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, (LIST 100_000, 50_000)) EQUALS 100_000
#ASSERT `the amount still recoverable within the limit for each passenger` 250_000 (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, EMPTY) EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT `the amount still recoverable within the limit for each passenger` 250_000 (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, (LIST 250_000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount still recoverable within the limit for each passenger` 250_000 (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, (LIST 200_000, 100_000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the court may at any stage make an order that is just and equitable in view of Article 22` (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may at any stage make an order that is just and equitable in view of Article 22` (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the court may award less than it would have awarded or make part of its award conditional on other proceedings` (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award less than it would have awarded or make part of its award conditional on other proceedings` (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award less than it would have awarded or make part of its award conditional on other proceedings` (`Limited Proceedings Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  EMPTY)

-- 6(4): the Minister's order.  Equivalent Facts: an order has been made, the equivalent of one unit in Singapore dollars.
#ASSERT `the sum in Singapore dollars` 250_000 (`Equivalent Facts` OF TRUE, 1.8) EQUALS 450_000
#ASSERT `the sum in Singapore dollars` 17 (`Equivalent Facts` OF TRUE, 1.8) EQUALS 30.6
#ASSERT REFUSED `the sum in Singapore dollars` 250_000 (`Equivalent Facts` OF FALSE, 0)

§§ `7. Notice of partial loss`

-- Partial Loss Facts: part is lost, date the remainder was received, date the whole was received.
#ASSERT `for Article 26(2) damage includes loss of part of the baggage or cargo`
#ASSERT `the date of receipt for Article 26(2)` (`Partial Loss Facts` OF TRUE,  YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 5
#ASSERT `the date of receipt for Article 26(2)` (`Partial Loss Facts` OF FALSE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1

§§ `8. Time for bringing proceedings`

`arrived on 1 March 2024` MEANS `the aircraft arrived at the destination` (YMD 2024 3 1)
`ought to have arrived on 1 March 2024` MEANS `the aircraft did not arrive` (YMD 2024 3 1)
`stopped on 1 March 2024` MEANS `the carriage stopped` (YMD 2024 3 1)

-- Employee Action Facts: arises out of damage to which a Convention relates, against the carrier's employee or agent, acting
-- within the scope of employment, how the carriage ended, the date the action or arbitration is brought.
#ASSERT NOT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `arrived on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `arrived on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `ought to have arrived on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `stopped on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, `arrived on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `arrived on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `section 8(1) bars the action against the employee or agent` (`Employee Action Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, `arrived on 1 March 2024`, YMD 2027 3 2)

#ASSERT NOT `Article 29 applies to proceedings for contribution between persons liable for damage to which a Convention relates`

-- Contribution Facts: seeks contribution for damage to which a Convention relates, the date of judgment or award, the date the
-- contribution action is brought, the last day allowed by the Limitation Act 1959 where it extends the time.
#ASSERT `the contribution action is in time` (`Contribution Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2024 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the contribution action is in time` (`Contribution Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2024 3 1, YMD 2026 3 2, NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the contribution action is in time` (`Contribution Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2024 3 1, YMD 2026 3 2, JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT `the contribution action is in time` (`Contribution Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2024 3 1, YMD 2026 6 1, JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the contribution action is in time` (`Contribution Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2024 3 1, YMD 2026 6 2, JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT `the contribution action is in time` (`Contribution Facts` OF FALSE, YMD 2024 3 1, YMD 2030 1 1, NOTHING)

§§ `9. Contributory negligence`

#ASSERT `the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953 is a law of Singapore under which a court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly for the purposes of Article 21`

§§ `10. Power to exclude aircraft in use for military purposes`

-- Military Facts: the Minister's order that s 10 applies to the State, carriage for the military authorities, aircraft registered in
-- that State, the whole capacity reserved.
#ASSERT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` (`Military Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` (`Military Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- the Warsaw Convention is not mentioned in s 10(2)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw Convention` (`Military Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` (`Military Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` (`Military Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` (`Military Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention does not apply to the carriage by reason of section 10` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` (`Military Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)

§§ `11. Actions against High Contracting Parties`

-- Party Action Facts: a High Contracting Party, has availed itself of the Additional Protocol, action in a Singapore court under
-- Article 28, claim in respect of carriage undertaken by the party, an enforcement order sought against its property.
#ASSERT `the High Contracting Party is deemed to have submitted to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` (`Party Action Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the High Contracting Party is deemed to have submitted to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` (`Party Action Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the High Contracting Party is deemed to have submitted to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` (`Party Action Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the High Contracting Party is deemed to have submitted to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` (`Party Action Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the High Contracting Party is deemed to have submitted to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` (`Party Action Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 11 authorises the issue of an enforcement order against the property of the High Contracting Party`

§§ `12. Application to carriage by air not governed by Warsaw (Hague) Convention and Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`

#ASSERT REFUSED `no regulations under section 12 applying the First and Third Schedules to carriage other than international carriage are encoded in this model`

§§ `13. Application to Government`

#ASSERT `this Act binds the Government`
